## 1 · Diagnose → `/app/agent-output/H16-history-dock/diagnosis.md`

Five breakage areas found (plus release hygiene), each grounded in the installed 0.1.2 host sources with `file:line` evidence:

| Card | Breakage |
|---|---|
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-composer-surface` | composer is now a Lexical editor on a `[data-composer-input]` contenteditable; the native textarea value-setter + synthetic `input` path is dead — writes go through the public `inputActions.setDraft` |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-composer-keydown` | document-level listener in `apply` with `event.target !== textarea` gating; the dock now renders *with* the resident composer, so the listener belongs in the dock component, on the editable host, deferring to the shell's CRITICAL Lexical keymap via `defaultPrevented` |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-session-history-source` | `SessionSnapshot` has no `nodes` and session-scope slots no longer receive a `session` prop; prompts must be folded from the durable event window (`ctx.sessions.binding(id).eventSource`, `user/message` with `source.kind === 'user'`) |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-client-inject` | `dsh-client-runtime` retired by the runtime split (scan of all 226 cached cohort manifests: 39 packages referenced it, last referencing version `0.1.1-rc.2`, zero `0.1.2+`); `slots` now comes from `dsh-client-ui-renderer`, `sessions` from `dsh-api-session-controller` |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-peer-cohort` | peers pinned to `^0.0.1-rc.1`; bumped to the cohort's `^0.1.2-alpha.2` (cordis `^4.0.2`), retired peer dropped, new providers added |

